"""Write the issue-specific portable technical receipt; no production edits."""
import hashlib,json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]/'Art/USA/buildings/usa_hq'
WORK=ROOT/'issue379'
def main():
    mast=json.loads((WORK/'mast_manifest.json').read_text())
    paths=[ROOT/'source/USA_HQ_Final.blend']+[ROOT/r['fbx'] for rs in mast['options'].values() for r in rs]+list((ROOT/'game').glob('SM_HQ_Shell*.fbx'))
    receipt={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)).replace('\\','/'):{'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for p in paths}
    (WORK/'delivery_hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2))
    recipe=json.loads((ROOT/'usa_hq.json').read_text())
    dependencies={'read_only_production_root':'/Game/Art/USA/Buildings/USAHQ','meshes':sorted({p['mesh'] for p in recipe['parts'] if p['name'] not in ('Shell','ShellDetail')}),'materials':sorted({v for m in recipe['meshes'].values() for v in m['slots'].values()}),'source_recipe_sha256':hashlib.sha256((ROOT/'usa_hq.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'instanced_section_estimate':sum(len(m['slots']) for m in recipe['meshes'].values())+6}
    (WORK/'preview_dependencies.json').write_text(json.dumps(dependencies,indent=2))
    lines=['# Issue 379 — mast review handoff','','**Visual review pending: choose 24, 28 or 32 m core height.** The source and saved preview use 28 m provisionally; this is not producer approval. Earlier stages remain approved: “All earlier HQ stages are approved; preserve every design except the masts.”','','[150 m options](renders/issue379/Height_Options_150m.png) · [Proportion overview](renders/issue379/Height_Options_Overview.png)','','| Option | Core / east tip Z (cm) | Beacon scale XYZ | Evidence |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
    for h,e,s in [(24,21,1.5),(28,24,1.75),(32,27,2)]:
        lines.append(f'| H{h} | {h*100} / {e*100} | {s:g} | [Master/game](renders/issue379/H{h}_review.png), [260 m pair](renders/issue379/H{h}_switch.png), [reference](renders/issue379/H{h}_reference_comparison.png) |')
    lines+=['','Core foot is **(-898.712, 0, 1151.000) cm**; east foot is **(-1090.000, -1995.000, 770.000) cm** in building space. Place meshes at these feet with identity rotation and scale 1. Tip XY equals foot XY; tip Z is above. Existing `SM_Beacon_Obstruction` is placed at each tip and scaled uniformly per table. Its existing red emissive material is reused.','','`MastTipCore` / `MastTipEast` empties sit on the rod tips; FBX helper nodes use the `SOCKET_` prefix. Local pivot is the mounting foot, not the mesh bounds centre. The east mounting pads extend slightly below that datum. **Drop the stale `MastTip` (-1080, 0, 1800) during integration**: it identifies neither new tip. Do not retain it as a third beacon attachment.','','## Portable delivery','','[Final source](source/USA_HQ_Final.blend); [all SHA-256 hashes](issue379/delivery_hashes.json); [exact per-LOD bounds, slots, tips and hashes](issue379/mast_manifest.json); [independent FBX reimport checks](issue379/fbx_reimport_checks.json). Recovery originals are in `issue379/baseline/`.','','| FBX (under this folder) | LOD | Triangles | SHA-256 |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
    for rs in mast['options'].values():
        for r in rs:
            p=r['fbx'].replace('\\','/');lines.append(f'| [{r["mesh"]}]({p}) | {r["lod"]} | {r["triangles"]:,} | `{receipt[p]["sha256"]}` |')
    lines+=['','Each mast/LOD uses the same three slots, in order: `HQ17_DarkStructure`, `HQ17_FramePaint`, `HQ17_TeamLight`, bound to the corresponding `MI_` instance under `/Game/Art/USA/Buildings/USAHQ/Materials/`. FramePaint and TeamLight remain; other original mast surfaces share DarkStructure. This mast-only material consolidation adds six sections to the established 74-section assembly, reaching its existing 80-section limit. No new textures. Existing texture sizes/settings are inherited, not re-authored.','','Both hand-made LOD1s retain every mast component, rung, rod and panel; radial cylinders become four-sided prisms, boxes remain. No automated collapse of the masts. Independently reimported FBXs have matching counts, pivots, helper positions and slots, one UV layer and zero degenerate mast triangles. Non-mast master meshes: **20,161 unchanged geometry/transform/material hashes**.','','## Shell and budget','','`Tools/Art/usa_hq_game_blender.py` now removes the recorded original mast surfaces before the shell/detail split and LOD generation; the three `game/` FBXs were re-exported. The surface mask accommodates triangulated/subdivided roof exports and rejects area mismatches; it does not remove a broad bounding box. The two fixed rooftop feeder-return pieces remain.','','| Mesh / measure | Old | New |','|---|---:|---:|','| Shell dense input FBX | 2,938,860 | 2,915,364 |','| Shell game LOD0 (engine reduction) | 274,000 | 267,000 |','| Shell game LOD1 (engine reduction) | 22,000 | 19,000 target |','| ShellDetail LOD0 | 42,096 | 41,344 |','| ShellDetail LOD1 | 11,878 | 11,436 |','| Separate core LOD0 / LOD1 | merged | 3,772 / 1,404 |','| Separate east LOD0 / LOD1 | merged | 5,780 / 2,700 |']
    for mode in ('game','far'):
        path=WORK/f'counts_{mode}.json'
        if path.exists():
            data=json.loads(path.read_text());lines.append(f'| Whole HQ {"LOD0" if mode=="game" else "LOD1"}, drawn instances | {347768 if mode=="game" else 39152:,} | **{data["total"]:,}** |')
    lines+=['','Dense FBX input is the reduction source, not the runtime mesh. The budgeted near/far shell reductions reserve room for the separate masts within 350,000 / 40,000 triangles. Counts include every door section and both beacons; per-component receipts are `issue379/counts_game.json` and `counts_far.json`. Use these measured counts instead of the older import report table.','','## Unreal evidence and integration boundary','','Candidate preview: `/Game/Art/Candidates/USA_HQ/Candidate22/L_HQ379_Masts`. Final masts: `Candidate22/FinalMasts/`. It reuses read-only production materials and unchanged moving meshes; it is not a self-contained production package. Native MCP lacks hand-authored LOD-file import, so LOD0/LOD1 mast FBXs are separate preview assets and all pieces are manually switched together. `Shells/SM_HQ379_ShellReview` contains dense master at index 0 and near reduction at index 1; `SM_HQ379_ShellFar` contains dense master at index 0 and far reduction at index 1. **Do not integrate these staging LOD indices as runtime settings.** Claude should import each selected pair as runtime LOD0/LOD1, reduce the stripped shell to the measured budgets, and update shared bounds/switch thresholds for the new tallest tip.','','Captures are actual **Unreal editor views**, not PIE/gameplay. Raw PNGs and camera JSON are beside the review images. Native capture renders horizontal FOV 90; a centred pixel crop gives effective FOV 60 at 16:9. 12 m is a mast-tip detail camera, 150/450 m target the building, and the switch pair uses arms 249.6/270.4 m. This demonstrates selected LOD appearances, not the automatic bounds-distance transition. `Tools/Art/usa_hq_379_preview.py` controls candidate-only poses/captures; `usa_hq_379_evidence.py` makes labelled crops/layouts without synthesis.','','Unverified / integration work: actual runtime camera, automatic synchronized 260 m switch with expanded bounds, beacon blink/power/ownership logic, collision/navigation/selection and representative GPU performance. Native socket serialization is not exposed by this MCP; FBX helpers were reimport-verified, while candidate beacon placement uses the documented transforms. Fresh-editor-process reload has not been verified. Existing shell-detail LOD1 import reports nearly-zero tangent/binormal warnings; no such warnings were reported for the final mast imports. No production setup, recipe/spec update, commit or push was performed.','','Claude starter after producer choice: “Use `$world-divide-building-production` for USA HQ #379. Read `Art/USA/buildings/usa_hq/HANDOFF_379.md`; use the producer-selected H24/H28/H32 pair and preserve all prior approvals. Integrate the supplied mast LOD pairs, stripped shells, new tip transforms, existing beacon/material bindings and updated budgets/bounds. Retire stale MastTip, update recipe/spec and validate runtime switch and beacon behaviour.”','']
    lines+=['## Mast bounds','','LOD0 local bounds in metres below; exact LOD1 bounds are in the linked manifest. Convert to Unreal cm and mirror Y when mapping the exported source coordinates.','','| Mesh | Local minimum (m) | Local maximum (m) |','|---|---|---|']
    for rs in mast['options'].values():
        for r in rs:
            if r['lod']==0:
                lo,hi=r['local_bounds_m'];fmt=lambda v:', '.join(f'{x:.3f}' for x in v)
                lines.append(f'| {r["mesh"]} | ({fmt(lo)}) | ({fmt(hi)}) |')
    lines[2]='**Chosen and visually approved: H28 — core 28 m, east 24 m; beacon scale 1.75.** Producer receipt (2026-10-22): “I opt for the middle (core 28, east 24)”. Source and saved preview use this option. Earlier stages remain approved: “All earlier HQ stages are approved; preserve every design except the masts.” Integration remains with Claude.'
    body='\n'.join(lines)+'\n'
    body=body.replace('19,000 target','19,000')
    body=body.replace('| Whole HQ LOD1, drawn instances | 39,152 |','| Whole HQ LOD1, drawn instances | 39,151 |')
    body=body.replace('| ShellDetail LOD1 | 11,878 | 11,436 |','| ShellDetail LOD1, FBX input | 11,878 | 11,436 |\n| ShellDetail LOD1, native preview import | 11,878 | 11,067 |')
    body=body.replace('Fresh-editor-process reload has not been verified.','Final mast packages and their material bindings were checked after a fresh editor process; the completed assembly is checked by saving and reloading its candidate level.')
    body=body.replace('Claude starter after producer choice:', 'Claude integration starter (chosen H28):')
    body=body.replace('producer-selected H24/H28/H32 pair','approved H28 pair (core 28 m, east 24 m)')
    body=body.replace('a centred pixel crop gives effective FOV 60 at 16:9.','a centred pixel crop gives effective FOV 60 at 16:9 for RTS views; proportion overviews retain the full vertical context.')
    body=body.replace('reaching its existing 80-section limit.','reaching its existing 80-section limit when production instancing is preserved. The preview uses individual actors and is not a draw-call benchmark; see `issue379/preview_dependencies.json`.')
    issue='**Known preview failure — not LOD acceptance:** the direct dense-to-19,000-triangle shell reduction loses exterior panels and produces a visible colour/surface change at the far switch. The supplied stripped dense shell and approved mast geometry are intact. Native `generate_lods` cannot set the production pipeline’s reduced LOD0 / progressive LOD1 settings; its property/UI tools did not expose those controls. Claude must rebuild through the existing `building_art.import_mesh` progressive path at 267,000 / 19,000 and revalidate the switch; this is not a claim that the progressive result is already proven. The captured far views are retained as failed evidence. Producer approval here covers the 28/24 m height choice, not this far-shell defect.'
    body=body.replace('## Unreal evidence and integration boundary','## Unreal evidence and integration boundary\n\n'+issue)
    body=body.replace('Use these measured counts instead of the older import report table.','Use these measured counts instead of the older import report table. `issue379/baseline_unreal_counts.json` records the live old asset counts. Native preview import removes 369 triangles from the detail LOD1; retaining all FBX triangles would put the far assembly at 39,813, still within 40,000.')
    body=body.replace('Existing `SM_Beacon_Obstruction` is placed at each tip and scaled uniformly per table.','Existing `SM_Beacon_Obstruction` is placed at each tip and scaled uniformly per table. The chosen beacon geometry extends 98 cm above its tip (56 cm source height × 1.75); cover at least Z=2898 cm when rebuilding the whole-building bounds. Reset inherited production bounds extensions before recalculating them.')
    final_detail=json.loads((ROOT/'game/game_meshes.json').read_text())['meshes']['SM_HQ_ShellDetail']['triangles'][1]
    body=body.replace('| ShellDetail LOD1, FBX input | 11,878 | 11,436 |\n| ShellDetail LOD1, native preview import | 11,878 | 11,067 |',f'| ShellDetail LOD1, final reimported FBX | 11,878 | {final_detail:,} |')
    body=body.replace('Native preview import removes 369 triangles from the detail LOD1; retaining all FBX triangles would put the far assembly at 39,813, still within 40,000.','The initial pre-export detail count included 369 faces discarded by FBX tessellation. Final counts now come from a round-trip of the exported mesh.')
    body=body.replace('Existing shell-detail LOD1 import reports nearly-zero tangent/binormal warnings; no such warnings were reported for the final mast imports.','The reported shell-detail tangent/binormal warnings were repaired: 65 UV faces corrected and 412 needle faces narrower than 1 mm removed; surviving face positions and material assignments are unchanged. Independent FBX reimport recomputes zero invalid tangent frames. See `issue379/tangent_repair.json`, `tangent_diagnostics.json`, and the fresh Unreal import receipt `unreal_tangent_import_check.json`. The candidate uses `Shells/SM_HQ_ShellDetail_LOD1_Final`; the older warning-producing staging asset is superseded.')
    body += '\nFinal warning fix: fresh native Unreal import of `SM_HQ_ShellDetail_LOD1_Final` passed with **zero tangent/binormal warnings**, 10,655 triangles. The selected H28 far captures were refreshed after this cleanup; H24/H32 far images retain the earlier 11,067-triangle detail mesh. The full shell generator was not rerun after the final sliver cleanup; its updated repair function was run on the delivered export and all 15 delivery FBXs were independently reimport-checked.\n'
    (ROOT/'HANDOFF_379.md').write_text(body,encoding='utf8')
    (WORK/'approval.json').write_text(json.dumps({'date':'2026-10-22','quote':'I opt for the middle (core 28, east 24)','chosen_option':'H28','core_tip_cm':2800,'east_tip_cm':2400,'beacon_scale':1.75,'state':'visual choice approved; production integration pending'},indent=2))
if __name__=='__main__':main()

